      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first six prime numbers.\n2. Calculate the sum of the first five prime numbers.\n3. Find the remainder when this sum is divided by the sixth prime number.\n\n**Step 1: Identify the first six prime numbers.**\n\nThe first six prime numbers are: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, and 13.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the sum of the first five prime numbers.**\n\nThe first five prime numbers are 2, 3, 5, 7, and 11. We sum these numbers:\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 = 28\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Find the remainder when the sum is divided by the sixth prime number.**\n\nThe sixth prime number is 13. We need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by 13. We perform the division:\n\\[\n28 \\div 13 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 2\n\\]\nThis can be written as:\n\\[\n28 = 13 \\times 2 + 2\n\\]\nThus, the remainder when 28 is divided by 13 is 2.\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
